# Force git to treat source as text even if it somehow contains a byte value
# that normally never appears in text (notably NUL). A single stray NUL byte in
# lib/csv.js once made git classify it as binary, so it could not be line-merged
# and a whole change was lost in the merge result.
#
# Deliberately only the `diff` attribute, NOT `text`/`eol`: the committed blobs
# already contain CRLF, so declaring `text eol=lf` would renormalize every file
# and bury real changes in a whitespace diff.
*.js    diff
*.json  diff
*.md    diff
*.html  diff
*.css   diff
*.csv   diff

# Genuinely binary.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
